> f(x: u8) = x >> (x+1)
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires 0 <= x + 1 < 8  (shift amount; C UB otherwise)
  defined at 8 of 256 points
  defined for: 0..6, 255
  undefined e.g. at x=7; x=8; x=9; x=10
  C undefined behaviour at 248 points, e.g. x=7
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range f
range of f -> u8:
  0..255   (2 distinct values)
  values: 0, 255
  fits in u8
  undefined at 248 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> wrap f
wrap analysis of f:
  x + 1   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=255
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=127
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 0 points, e.g. 
      exact for: 0..6
  over all 256 points of the domain
> equiv f f
f and f are equal on the domain of f (exhaustive)
